expectation e_2ea25e8cda4d2d78 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="litterae keeps expectations explicit" detail="litterae should keep project expectations in an authored expectations.susu sidecar so implementation evidence and intent can be reviewed together.";
expectation e_ee705788dc2f4a20 target=project subject=- status=proposed source="human:maintainer" title="litterae documents primary workflows" detail="litterae should describe the business or product workflows that matter most, then link those expectations to observed files, symbols, or workflows as evidence improves.";
expectation e_0cf9ce3bfb208414 target=project subject=- status=proposed source="human:maintainer" title="litterae records verification evidence" detail="litterae should record how important expectations are checked, such as tests, CI runs, manual reviews, policy checks, runtime traces, or release approvals.";
expectation e_25466c712a403a7c target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:justin" title="litterae reacts to SIGTERM, not just SIGINT" detail="The server process must catch SIGTERM (sent by docker stop and systemd) alongside SIGINT and run the same graceful-shutdown path, since the deployed environment (susumu.dev) stops the container via SIGTERM, not Ctrl-C.";
expectation e_5989aadcf3a862fc target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:justin" title="mail app surfaces action failures via toast, not inline red text" detail="Compose send/save, contact save/delete, message snooze/nudge/download, and mailbox pagination failures show a dismissible bottom-of-screen toast (web/src/lib/Toast.svelte + toast.svelte.ts) instead of a per-component inline red <p>. Initial-page-load failures (mailbox list, message view) stay as persistent inline empty/error states on purpose -- a toast would auto-dismiss over a blank page with no explanation left behind.";
expectation e_f25bbb76fd20f7c4 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:justin" title="SMTP HELO/EHLO argument is validated, not stored verbatim" detail="Inbound and submission SMTP reject a HELO/EHLO argument that isn't a valid domain name or RFC 5321 address literal ([ip] / [IPv6:ip]) with a 501 reply, instead of storing it verbatim. The rejected value must not be used for SPF checks or audit logging, and a valid HELO sent afterward on the same connection must still succeed.";
expectation e_b1507bcc102fed8e target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:justin" title="A single account cannot send unbounded outbound mail" detail="Per-account outbound sending (via submission SMTP or JMAP EmailSubmission) is capped at 200 messages and 500 recipients per rolling hour, enforced inside queue::enqueue so both paths share one check. A leaked password or app password must not be able to blast unlimited mail and burn the whole instance's sending reputation. DSNs are exempt since they're generated locally, not by an authenticated sender. Submission reports a rate-limited send as SMTP 450 (temporary), distinct from the generic 451 local-error reply.";
expectation e_cc4230a723d9a38a target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:justin" title="One source IP cannot exhaust smtp-in's global connection limit" detail="smtp-in enforces a per-source-IP concurrent connection cap (32) alongside the existing global 512-connection semaphore. Without this, a single IP holding all 512 slots denies the listener to every other sender -- the global cap alone only protects against exhausting total capacity, not one source monopolizing it.";
expectation e_a215eef49000e34f target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:justin" title="web/ has zero known npm audit vulnerabilities" detail="postcss is bumped past the high-severity path-traversal/source-map-disclosure advisory (GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849) via a plain dependency bump. cookie is pinned to ^0.7.2 via an npm 'overrides' entry to clear the low-severity out-of-bounds-character advisory (GHSA-pxg6-pf52-xh8x), since @sveltejs/kit's own dependency on cookie ^0.6.0 hasn't been bumped upstream in any published 2.x release; overriding the transitive dependency is safe since the 0.6->0.7 change only tightened input validation, not the parse/serialize API.";
